<title>USA: Top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</title>
<headline>Top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following were the top 10 movies at the box office over the weekend, according to studio estimates collected by Exhibitor Relations Co. Inc. Final data are due Monday. (Rank last week in parentheses).</p>
<p>    1 (*) The Relic ........................ $9.4 million</p>
<p>    2(20) Evita ............................ $8.6 million</p>
<p>    3 (1) Michael .......................... $8.5 million</p>
<p>    4 (2) Jerry Maguire .................... $7.8 million</p>
<p>    5 (3) Scream ........................... $7.6 million</p>
<p>    6 (*) Jackie Chan's First Strike ....... $6.5 million</p>
<p>    7(22) The People Vs. Larry Flynt ....... $5.6 million</p>
<p>    8 (*) Turbulence ....................... $4.4 million</p>
<p>    9 (5) One Fine Day ..................... $3.6 million</p>
<p>   10 (6) Beavis and Butt-head Do America .. $3.0 million</p>
<p>NOTE: &quot;The Relic&quot; and &quot;Beavis and Butt-head Do America&quot; are released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc..</p>
<p>&quot;Evita&quot; was produced by Cinergi Pictures Entertainment Inc and released by Walt Disney Co..</p>
<p>&quot;Michael&quot; was produced by Turner Pictures, and released by New Line Cinema, both units of Time Warner Inc.</p>
<p>&quot;Jerry Maguire&quot; is released by TriStar Pictures, a unit of Sony Corp..</p>
<p>&quot;Scream&quot; is released by Disney-owned Miramax Films.</p>
<p>&quot;Jackie Chan's First Strike&quot; was released by New Line.</p>
<p>&quot;The People Vs. Larry Flynt&quot; was released by Sony-owned Columbia Pictures.</p>
<p>&quot;Turbulence&quot; was released by MGM, which is owned by financier Kirk Kerkorian and Australia's Seven Network Ltd. &quot;One Fine Day&quot; is released by 20th Century Fox, a unit of News Corp.</p>
</text>
